--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WEB PARITY — date pipeline reproduced from the source (NOT a "corrected" version)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  looksLikeISO(v)        = ISO_RFC3339_RE.test(v) && Number.isFinite(Date.parse(v))
                           — verbatim regex + a non-lenient DateFormatter that rejects impossible
                             calendar dates (2024-02-31 / month 13 / hour 25), exactly like Date.parse.
  format(iso)            = port of dateFormat.formatDateTime → locale medium-date + short-time,
                           "—" sentinel for an unparseable value (the universal web fallback).
  rfc3339(from: Date)    = port of localInputToRfc3339 → UTC RFC 3339 instant ("…Z", second precision).
  seed(now)              = yesterday at 12:00 local (the command-palette open seed).
  phases                 = error > loading(isLoading && asOf==nil) > historical(asOf!=nil) >
                           prompt(pickerOpen) > withdrawn  (web guardrail order + sanctioned P4 leaves).
  title (prompt mode)    = rendered with an empty `when`, matching the web AlertBanner title literally.

  States reproduced (every presented one renders — no hidden surface): withdrawn (web `return null`
  gate), loading (skeleton), prompt (pick-a-time empty-equivalent, never a blank box), historical
  (read-only banner + Return-to-live + inline picker), error (retry). Orthogonal connection axis
  live/stale/offline → freshness chip + banner + one-shot stale auto-refresh.

  i18n keys (resolve through the P1/S10 facade — no English literals in Swift):
    timeMachine.banner.title|body|pickPrompt|pick|returnToLive|submit|cancel|inputLabel  (web parity)
    timeMachine.surfaceLabel|live|stale|offline|staleBanner|offlineBanner|refresh|loadingA11y|
    errorTitle|retry                                                                     (native chrome)

